  "reasoning_log_text": "The study strongly supports hierarchical predictive coding. H2 factors (13-24) are well supported: Feedforward Ascending Gamma, Directed Connectivity, and Error Propagation were strongly evidenced (1.0). H1 factors show moderate support for suppression mechanisms like Habituation and Activity Suppression (0.6). H3 Ubiquity is supported regarding Hierarchical Presence (1.0) and Order Stability (0.8). The use of the Local-Global paradigm directly addresses hierarchical structure, and frequency specificity (g/a/b bands) is detailed. Specific quantitative results support PE1 in the early auditory cortex (g-band, bottom-up) and PE2/updates in higher cortices (a/b band, top-down). The study explicitly disproves a purely non-hierarchical model (1.0 for the contrast between unpredicted local novelty and predicted local novelty). Correlation analysis confirmed PE2 drives Component 3 (updates) across trials."
